	(text "B  ESC signals and servo"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.14 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "02b76234-cc0f-5b85-bf96-67584b9d7e41")
	)
	(text "1. Battery: 2S LiPo, 6.0-8.4 V (ESC LVC cuts at 6.0 V).\n   T-plug pigtail (12 AWG bare ends) soldered to J1 pads;\n   pad size TBD (footprint is the 2.5 mm2 placeholder).\n2. ESC is powered OFF-BOARD: battery -> ESC on its own\n   12 AWG leads (up to 20 A). This board carries only its\n   own loads (about 7.3 A worst case), so F1 is sized for\n   that, not for the motor.\n3. All fuses and protection values TBD.\n4. Single common GND; star point at J1 in layout.\n5. +6V_BEC is ESC-supplied (servo only), never joined\n   to a 5 V rail.\n6. Signals are 3.3 V logic or lower.\n7. U1 Pololu D36V50F5: all 12 pins drawn (2x VIN, 2x VOUT,\n   4x GND, 2x VRP, EN, PG). VRP unused (sensor buck fed\n   from VBAT via F4). EN left unconnected: the module's\n   internal pull-up keeps it on (ESP32 EN control\n   archived). PG: open-drain, to ESP32 via J5 (ESP32\n   INPUT_PULLUP, non-strapping GPIO TBD).\n8. U2 EN per module datasheet (TBD); U2 footprint TBD.\n9. Rails are project power symbols (rc_power lib):\n   pin name = Value = net name.\n10. PWR_FLAG = ERC marker only (no part, not on the PCB):\n    tells ERC where power enters VBAT_RAW, GND, VBAT,\n    VIN_CPU, VIN_SENS, LDO_IN, +6V_BEC.\n11. Net classes (kicad_pro): HighCurrent = *VBAT*, GND;\n    Power5A = +5V_CPU, *VIN_CPU;\n    Power3A = +5V_SENS, *VIN_SENS, *+6V_BEC.\n12. J6/J7: 2-wire USB-C pigtails (20 AWG, 30 cm, about\n    0.10 V drop at 5 A; trim to 10-15 cm) into the Pi 5\n    and ESP32 USB-C inputs, keeping their own input\n    protection. Pi 5 gets no USB-PD 5 A offer (USB ports\n    limited to 600 mA unless set in config.txt)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 320.04 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4da2a275-10ec-502e-b684-7bb57d615234")
	)
	(text "ESC power does NOT pass through this board:\nbattery -> ESC on its own 12 AWG leads.\nJ1/F1 carry only the board loads\n(about 7.3 A worst case at 6.4 V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 114.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "537cac65-0f14-5eda-89a6-76b089f31ff2")
	)
